 | `APERTAR_DNG_DONTNEED=sync` or `off` | writer | When a written DNG's pages leave the page cache: `writer` right after the write (as before; the pages are still dirty then, so the call frees nothing and costs a cross-CPU LRU drain per frame), `sync` on the once-a-second sync thread after the file's `fsync` (cDNG only; lossy DNG then behaves as `off`), `off` never. |
 | `APERTAR_DNG_WRITEBACK=0` | on | No `sync_file_range` per written DNG (the kernel's own writeback only). |
 | `APERTAR_MEDIA_SYNC_MS=0` | 1000 | No once-a-second `fsync` of the finished DNGs and the clip folder during a take; the stop-time `syncfs` stays. |
+| `APERTAR_WEB_PREVIEW_RECORDING_FPS=N` | 30 | The WebUI live preview's frame rate while a raw take runs (`0` pauses it). Its downsample runs on libcamera's completion thread, inside the per-frame cycle, whenever a browser shows the preview (about 0.2 to 0.5 ms per frame). |
 | `APERTAR_RT=1` | off | The start script runs the whole Core process under `SCHED_FIFO` priority 70 on cores 1 to 3 with the best-effort I/O class (`APERTAR_RT_PRIORITY`, `APERTAR_RT_CPUS` adjust it), as cinemate runs cinepi-raw. An A/B instrument, not a recommendation: equal-priority FIFO threads never preempt each other, so the capture thread can wait behind FIFO writers. Needs `LimitRTPRIO` on the unit: install `config/apertar-core-capture-priority.conf` as a drop-in. |
 | `APERTAR_MEDIA_TUNE=1` | off | Kernel-side knobs for the recording drive through the `apertar-media-tune` root helper (dirty-page cushion, scheduler, queue depth). |
 
diff --git a/src/ApertarCoreApp.cpp b/src/ApertarCoreApp.cpp
index 34687b2..a28c734 100644
--- a/src/ApertarCoreApp.cpp
+++ b/src/ApertarCoreApp.cpp
@@ -79,6 +79,25 @@ constexpr uint32_t kWebPreviewMaxWidth = 640;
 constexpr uint32_t kWebPreviewMaxHeight = 360;
 constexpr double kWebPreviewMaxFps = 30.0;
 constexpr int kWebPreviewJpegQuality = 75;
+
+// The web preview's rate while a raw take runs (APERTAR_WEB_PREVIEW_RECORDING_FPS): default the normal 30,
+// 0 = no web preview frames while recording. The downsample for it runs on libcamera's completion thread
+// (about 0.2 to 0.5 ms per frame measured idle in the kb), so this is the A/B knob for its share of the
+// WebUI-open drops (kb working/dng-chain, V/H4).
+double webPreviewRecordingFps()
+{
+    static const double fps = []() {
+        const char *text = std::getenv("APERTAR_WEB_PREVIEW_RECORDING_FPS");
+        if (!text || !*text)
+            return kWebPreviewMaxFps;
+        char *end = nullptr;
+        const double parsed = std::strtod(text, &end);
+        if (end == text || *end != '\0' || !std::isfinite(parsed) || parsed < 0.0 || parsed > kWebPreviewMaxFps)
+            return kWebPreviewMaxFps;
+        return parsed < 0.5 ? 0.0 : parsed;
+    }();
+    return fps;
+}
 constexpr size_t kMaxEditableHardwareConfigBytes = 256 * 1024;
 
